<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Arabic, for drivers on the Iraq and Syria corridor.

    Modern Standard, matching the consignee's tracking page: the readers share
    no spoken dialect but all read the register their customs paperwork and
    waybills are already written in.

    Two choices a translator would ask about, kept consistent with the web page:

      الشاحنة (the lorry) rather than المركبة (the vehicle). The Turkish "araç"
      is generic, but the person reading this is sitting in a specific truck.

      Numbers arrive already formatted with Latin digits — see formatRemaining,
      which is pinned to Locale.ROOT — so nothing here should reintroduce
      Arabic-Indic numerals. A distance in ٨٫٣ beside a plate reading 27 AB 100
      looks broken, and the plate is never transliterated.

    The app_name is deliberately NOT translated. It is what the driver looks for
    in a launcher full of icons, and what a dispatcher says down a phone.
-->
